// An end-to-end spec puts focus on a locator through `focusOn(target)` and
// presses a key on it through `pressKey(target, key)` in
// tests/e2e/windowKeys.ts (docs/e2e-contracts.md, "Input waits for focus").
// A bare `await target.focus()` returns before focus has moved - into a
// card's or a panel's frame it lands a moment later - and the key pressed
// on the next line goes to whatever held focus, the loss behind the
// keyboard journeys that failed on a loaded Mac. Both helpers wait until
// the target holds the window's focus and take their turn behind any other
// input to the page. A `focus()` inside a script run in the page
// (`evaluate`) is the page's own and is never awaited, so it stays. The
// helper files (everything in tests/e2e that is not a *.spec.ts) are
// exempt. Runs inside `pnpm check` through biome.json's plugins, as an
// error since every spec moved.

language js

`await $target.focus($...)` where {
  $filename <: r".*tests/e2e/[^/]*\.spec\.ts",
  register_diagnostic(span=$target, message="A bare focus() returns before focus has landed, and the key pressed next goes where focus still is. Use focusOn(target), or pressKey(target, key) to press on it, from tests/e2e/windowKeys.ts: they wait until the target holds the window's focus (docs/e2e-contracts.md, Input waits for focus).", severity="error")
}
